00:52:54.420 --> 00:52:56.060
so that you know, you know,

00:52:56.060 --> 00:52:58.680
you're getting a good back and forth,

00:52:58.680 --> 00:53:00.940
and then meet somewhere
in the sensible middle.

00:53:00.940 --> 00:53:04.310
So I think she's a productive
part of the conversation,

00:53:04.310 --> 00:53:06.540
even when I don't agree with her.

00:53:06.540 --> 00:53:07.410
- All right, let's shift.

00:53:07.410 --> 00:53:08.550
- Let me give you a test.
- Yes.

00:53:08.550 --> 00:53:10.346
- Here's a test.
- Okay.

00:53:10.346 --> 00:53:13.343
- A very simple test to find
out if she's smart or not.

00:53:14.210 --> 00:53:15.900
The answer to climate change,

00:53:15.900 --> 00:53:18.300
even if you don't think it's a problem,

00:53:18.300 --> 00:53:22.080
is generation for nuclear, or
at least being pro-nuclear.

00:53:22.080 --> 00:53:24.060
If you see her never come out

00:53:24.060 --> 00:53:25.950
in favor of nuclear as part of--

00:53:25.950 --> 00:53:27.070
- Ah, I like where you're going with this.

00:53:27.070 --> 00:53:28.550
- As part of the solution,

00:53:28.550 --> 00:53:30.650
then she has abandoned reason.

00:53:30.650 --> 00:53:33.780
Because even the people
on her side, Corey Booker,

00:53:33.780 --> 00:53:36.070
there's several people
running for president.

00:53:36.070 --> 00:53:37.550
- Most of them are not, thought, right?

00:53:37.550 --> 00:53:38.383
Most of them are not.

00:53:38.383 --> 00:53:39.730
- It's half and half, or something.

00:53:39.730 --> 00:53:42.830
I think three I know, I can't
